Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
> On 15.04.2012 09:25, Patric Mueller wrote:
>> 
>> For example in SporkHack and UnNetHack, you encounter much more lava
>> in Gehennom as those forks have been replaced the filler maze levels
>> with open mines-like levels that have lava rivers running across the
>> level.
>
> Are the probabilities for wands of cold adjusted in those variants?

Not for UnNetHack and AFAIK also not for SporkHack. I think it's also
not necessary as there are quite a few options open to the player if
there really is a shortage of wands of cold (although I think even in
SporkHack [there are fewer lava levels in UnNetHack because of Heck^2]
2 fully charged wands should be more than enough).

> Or is having levitation (or fireproof water walking[*]) now crucial?

Not at all. There are myriads of ways in NetHack to cross a few
squares of lava.

You already mentioned two additional ones yourself. Then you also can
use jumping, a flying steed, teleportation (not with the Amulet
though), luring a cold-breathing monster to it, using taxi-monsters,
or depending on the layout of the level you can dig around the lava
(when the different pockets of the mines-like levels are touching).

I'm certain this is not a full list of possible actions and there are
even more.

> [*] In case that works; I've never tried.

Yes, that works already in vanilla, although items in your inventory
might burn up and you will get some damage if you are not fire
resistant.

